						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=665.msg5753#msg5753"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=665.msg5753#msg5753">Re:Einalem /Breneaur</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #12 on:</b> February 25, 2004, 05:27:24 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							That&#039;s the most you can expect out of a guild, so yeah, great way to handle it on Ap&#039;s part. &nbsp;It&#039;s not like they can force the guy to give the account back. &nbsp;All they can do is talk about it and guildremove him. <br /><br />I&#039;m surprised he gave it back. &nbsp;He could have denied everything or just done the equivalent of &quot;neener neener! mine now!&quot; &nbsp;Of course he might have had trouble getting into a high end guild on rodcet nife afterward. &nbsp;Though that could still be a problem. &nbsp;<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/smiley1.gif" alt="Smiley" border="0" /> &nbsp;<br /><br />I&#039;m sorry that happened to you, Az, and I can see why you&#039;re going to stop using the account even though you have it back now. &nbsp;Who knows when this guy could just decide to steal back his account again, only this time jump servers or something? &nbsp;Get what you can off of it and cancel the account. &nbsp;:(
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
